00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:37.246
- Like real personal life where,

00:00:37.246 --> 00:00:38.815
we changed enough details that,

00:00:38.815 --> 00:00:41.555
I wouldn't get angry phone calls.

00:00:41.555 --> 00:00:42.388
Hopefully.

00:00:42.388 --> 00:00:43.500
- I think people wish
I'd do that with songs.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:44.333
(Kelly and Anna laugh)

00:00:44.333 --> 00:00:45.166
- Whoops!

00:00:45.166 --> 00:00:45.999
Sorry!

00:00:45.999 --> 00:00:46.832
- [Kelly] Sorry!

00:00:46.832 --> 00:00:47.665
- Shouldn't have messed up.

00:00:47.665 --> 00:00:48.498
- [Kelly] Truth.

00:00:48.498 --> 00:00:49.816
- Then you wouldn't be in a song.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:51.149
- Not my fault.

00:00:52.474 --> 00:00:54.010
- But the second season,

00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:56.215
it's one of those funny things where,

00:00:56.215 --> 00:00:58.048
even though it's about

00:00:59.007 --> 00:01:02.127
a guy who's a different
race, different gender,

00:01:02.127 --> 00:01:03.470
different point in his life.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:06.278
It starts with him, unlike my season,

00:01:06.278 --> 00:01:08.517
it starts with him in his thirties

00:01:08.517 --> 00:01:09.390
and his life blows up.

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:10.223
Relatable.

00:01:11.073 --> 00:01:12.953
And then it's sort of,
oh, I'm starting over.

00:01:12.953 --> 00:01:15.063
I thought my- I found my person,

00:01:15.063 --> 00:01:18.076
but instead, I'm on a love life journey--

00:01:18.076 --> 00:01:19.300
- This is so unrelatable!

00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:20.133
- I know!

00:01:20.133 --> 00:01:20.966
How would anyone--

00:01:20.966 --> 00:01:22.096
- Says who would relate to this?

00:01:22.096 --> 00:01:24.152
- And it's, but you know,

00:01:24.152 --> 00:01:26.701
the Olivia Rodrigo stuff of, oh my gosh,

00:01:26.701 --> 00:01:28.731
you can be 17 and feeling
all the same stuff.

00:01:28.731 --> 00:01:32.032
And then, you know, this new season is,

00:01:32.032 --> 00:01:34.020
is, you're a grown person,

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:37.928
but you're still humiliating
yourself for love.

00:01:37.928 --> 00:01:39.988
And you know, just you're moping around

00:01:39.988 --> 00:01:40.821
when your heart is broken--

00:01:40.821 --> 00:01:42.375
- I'd rather be that person than Jaden.

00:01:42.375 --> 00:01:43.678
I'd rather humiliate myself--

00:01:43.678 --> 00:01:44.802
- Totally!

00:01:44.802 --> 00:01:46.058
- Absolutely run into the humiliation.

00:01:46.058 --> 00:01:47.227
- Run, just head on.

00:01:47.227 --> 00:01:48.060
(Kelly laughs)

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:48.893
- That's really the message--

00:01:48.893 --> 00:01:49.726
- That's my advice--

00:01:49.726 --> 00:01:50.927
- This new season, yeah.

00:01:50.927 --> 00:01:51.760
- That's the tagline.

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:54.004
- Run towards humiliation,
Love Life Season 2.

00:01:54.004 --> 00:01:54.837
(Kelly Laughs)

00:01:54.837 --> 00:01:55.891
- When we've talked about this before,

00:01:55.891 --> 00:01:57.531
but you started acting
when you were pretty young.

00:01:57.531 --> 00:01:58.364
Right?

00:01:58.364 --> 00:01:59.197
- Yeah.

00:01:59.197 --> 00:02:01.419
- I kind of heard crazy
stories of how you used to be

00:02:01.419 --> 00:02:04.267
young and traveled to New
York, without parents.

00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:05.100
- Yeah.

00:02:05.100 --> 00:02:07.146
So I grew up in Maine and I started

00:02:07.146 --> 00:02:08.742
auditioning for Broadway shows and stuff

00:02:08.742 --> 00:02:11.696
when I was 10 and around, and basically

00:02:11.696 --> 00:02:13.040
that would mean my
parents have to drive me

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:15.806
five hours to New York
for one audition and then

00:02:15.806 --> 00:02:17.779
come home, which was just not sustainable.

00:02:17.779 --> 00:02:19.588
You know, they both worked full time.

00:02:19.588 --> 00:02:21.921
And so eventually around 12,

00:02:22.836 --> 00:02:24.503
my brother was 14 and they were like,

00:02:24.503 --> 00:02:26.237
"You guys can get on a
Greyhound bus and go to

00:02:26.237 --> 00:02:28.697
New York City and come
back and you'll be fine."

00:02:28.697 --> 00:02:30.925
- Not a Dateline special
in the way they talked.

00:02:30.925 --> 00:02:31.758
- [Anna] Yeah!

00:02:31.758 --> 00:02:33.016
- Yeah, no.

00:02:33.016 --> 00:02:33.849
- But yeah.

00:02:33.849 --> 00:02:35.617
So when I went and
auditioned for High Society,

00:02:35.617 --> 00:02:37.995
which was the show that I eventually did,

00:02:37.995 --> 00:02:39.991
they, you know, I get on a Greyhound bus

00:02:39.991 --> 00:02:41.091
with my brother, I audition.

00:02:41.091 --> 00:02:43.092
and they're like, "Okay. So we want to

00:02:43.092 --> 00:02:45.127
call you back for tomorrow."

00:02:45.127 --> 00:02:46.649
Very exciting.

00:02:46.649 --> 00:02:48.860
And they were like, "So
we'll see you tomorrow."

00:02:48.860 --> 00:02:49.723
And I was like, "Yes, you will.

00:02:49.723 --> 00:02:50.694
Because I live here."

00:02:50.694 --> 00:02:51.527
Totally.

00:02:51.527 --> 00:02:52.360
(Kelly Laughs)

00:02:52.360 --> 00:02:53.468
Absolutely.

00:02:53.468 --> 00:02:54.767
I am not a homeless street rat,

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:57.440
running around the streets of New York.

00:02:57.440 --> 00:02:58.523
So my parents

00:02:59.451 --> 00:03:01.235
faxed a credit card,

00:03:01.235 --> 00:03:03.307
a copy of the credit card to a hotel.

00:03:03.307 --> 00:03:04.693
And they were, our children will be

00:03:04.693 --> 00:03:06.597
checking in and then
we'll be along shortly

00:03:06.597 --> 00:03:08.105
because obviously we're
not terrible parents

00:03:08.105 --> 00:03:09.687
who've let them go to New York.

00:03:09.687 --> 00:03:10.664
- Oh my gosh I love your parents.

00:03:10.664 --> 00:03:12.155
- And so we know walk
in and we're like, "Yes,

00:03:12.155 --> 00:03:14.103
our parents will be along shortly." And--

00:03:14.103 --> 00:03:14.936
- It's clearly--

00:03:14.936 --> 00:03:16.833
- And we like wash our socks
and underwear in the sink.

00:03:16.833 --> 00:03:18.707
And then, just go back in the next day.

00:03:18.707 --> 00:03:21.266
And just all the while pretending, yes,

00:03:21.266 --> 00:03:23.384
I am a totally normal
person who lives here

00:03:23.384 --> 00:03:24.217
and I'm not--

00:03:24.217 --> 00:03:25.162
(Kelly Laughs)

00:03:25.162 --> 00:03:26.772
- I just came from my home.

00:03:26.772 --> 00:03:29.063
Your brother's awesome
to take you to do that.

00:03:29.063 --> 00:03:29.896
It's so cool.

00:03:29.896 --> 00:03:30.729
- Yeah

00:03:30.729 --> 00:03:31.562
- Yeah, we're having a
(indistinct) for my brother.

00:03:31.562 --> 00:03:33.525
- That's so, and I mean,
it's just so funny.

00:03:33.525 --> 00:03:35.191
Cause when you have kids,
I'm going to ask you

00:03:35.191 --> 00:03:36.743
if you would allow your
kid, because I would

00:03:36.743 --> 00:03:38.014
never allow my kids to
do what I did when I

00:03:38.014 --> 00:03:38.847
was young.

00:03:38.847 --> 00:03:40.730
It was like, "Oh just
be home before dark."

00:03:40.730 --> 00:03:41.637
- Oh, I wouldn't even allow
my kids to be sick on me

00:03:41.637 --> 00:03:43.647
- the way that you that you would so...

00:03:43.647 --> 00:03:44.480
- I know.

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:45.313
You would.

00:03:45.313 --> 00:03:46.146
- So maybe I'd be the kind of person who

00:03:46.146 --> 00:03:47.421
would be like, "Have fun sweetie!

00:03:47.421 --> 00:03:48.936
Bye!

00:03:48.936 --> 00:03:49.999
Good Luck!"

00:03:49.999 --> 00:03:51.065
(Kelly laughs)

00:03:51.065 --> 00:03:52.818
- That's amazing

00:03:52.818 --> 00:03:55.479
"Don't talk to strangers!"

00:03:55.479 --> 00:03:57.423
So wait, you tweeted this a while ago,

00:03:57.423 --> 00:03:59.832
